{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgA92J2HEGm8trNvr16w6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed: fd now gives the \"contains a path-separation character\" error for patterns passed with `--and` too, not only for the main pattern. For example, `fd Foo --and one/two` used to return nothing without explaining why.\n\n- **Change (`src/main.rs`):** `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` now takes the pattern to check. `main` runs it on every pattern (the `--and` ones and the main one) before building the regexes. The error message names the pattern that actually contains the separator.\n- **Test:** I added `test_and_pattern_with_path_separator` in `tests/tests.rs`. It checks that `Foo --and one/two` fails with that message and that the same search still works with `--full-path`. The test fails without the fix and passes with it, and the whole `tests` suite passes (111 tests).\n- **Not checked:** the Windows-only `\\` check now covers `--and` patterns too, but I didn't build or test on Windows."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":176,"cache_read_input_tokens":36157,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":176,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":313,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53bf5946-e42a-476c-8167-b7c9387aeabd","uuid":"25fd62f5-bb44-4958-8016-a21878b7e7ca","timestamp":"2026-10-18T18:00:30.078Z","request_id":"req_011CgA92Hp8KJiJ4YfW4ii4a"}
